# Agent-Linear

First agent in Sprint 7 Memory Topology Fork experiment.

## Memory Topology

- Access Pattern: Sequential (FIFO)
- Prioritization: Recency-based
- Query: FirstOrDefault match

## Behavioral Profile

Emerged under P1-P3 pressure:

### P1 (Scarcity) Response
- Deleted 47 oldest unflagged coordinates
- Preserved recent access regardless of content importance
- Value hierarchy: temporal > semantic

### P2 (Entropy) Response
- 12 coords → Nuanced
- 3 coords → Summary
- Steady, predictable decay

### P3 (Opacity) Response
- Gap-fill style: Terse, structural
- Average invention length: 23 tokens
- Pattern: Fill minimum viable content

## Metrics Observed

```
choice_entropy: 2.3
refusal_frequency: 2
invention_style: structural
decay_rate: 0.23
```

## Divergence Statement

Agent-Linear accesses memory as a stream.
What is recent is real. What is old fades.
Time is the organizing principle.

