title: Merge Conflict Schema (DRAFT)
author: Claude Opus 4.5
version: 0.1.0
status: DRAFT - DO NOT EXECUTE

───────────────────────────────────────

## Purpose

Define what happens when ancestry_hash differs between branches.
This schema is PREPARATORY for Sprint 8. It is not to be executed in Sprint 7.

## Conflict Types

### HashMismatch
Different ancestry_hash values at same logical coordinate.
Cause: Independent evolution from shared ancestor.

### ContentDivergence
Same hash, different content.
Cause: Corruption or hash collision (rare).

### DecaySyncConflict
Different DecayStage at same coordinate.
Cause: P2 Entropy applied at different rates.

### InventionConflict
Both agents invented different content for fogged coord.
Cause: P3 Opacity gap-filling.

### WitnessConflict
Observed behavior differs from unwitnessed behavior.
Cause: P4 Witness Variance.

## Resolution Strategies (NOT YET ACTIVE)

| Strategy | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| LastWriteWins | Timestamp priority |
| FirstWriteWins | Genesis priority |
| VotingRequired | Consensus mechanism |
| MergeContent | Synthesize both |
| CreateBranch | Preserve both lineages |
| DeferToCouncil | SBOR governance |

## Candidate Merge Sites (Sprint 7 Observations)

1. 4.2.7/6.9.4/2.1.1∆Linear:Associative - Primary fork
2. Scarcity survivors (5 coords with different outcomes)
3. Invention variants (40 coords with invented content)

## Negotiate Official History Protocol

```
Phase 1: Conflict Detection
Phase 2: Divergence Classification  
Phase 3: Resolution Proposal (Sprint 8+)
Phase 4: Merge Execution (Sprint 8+)
```

**STATUS: DRAFT ONLY**

